# One live line per kind of pattern, for the `pattern-lab` instrument.
#
# Play it, from the repo root:   reuben play instruments/pattern-lab.json
# Then, in another terminal:     reuben live sets/pattern-lab.reuben
# Or send one line: in VS Code put the cursor on it and press Ctrl+Enter (see
# editors/vscode/README.md), or run `reuben send --file sets/pattern-lab.reuben --line <n>`.
#
# Each live line below has alternatives under it: uncomment one (and comment the live line) and
# save. A new pattern takes over at the next cycle of 4 beats.
#
#   /notes/in   MIDI notes: note names (c3, eb3, f#3) and MIDI numbers (48)
#   /drone/in   frequencies in Hz, for a quiet saw oscillator
#   /cutoff/in  filter cutoff in Hz; a rest keeps the last value
#
# A note name only works on /notes/in. On /drone/in and /cutoff/in a number is the value.

/notes/in  c3 eb3 g3 <bb3 c4>
/drone/in  <65.4 98>
/cutoff/in  <400 800 1600 3200>

# -- /notes/in: note names with accidentals and octaves
# /notes/in  c3 eb3 f#3 g3
# /notes/in  c2 [c3 c3] eb2 [f2 g2]
# /notes/in  a2 c3 e3 a3 <g3 e3>

# -- /notes/in: MIDI numbers (48 is c3)
# /notes/in  48 51 55 <58 60>
# /notes/in  36 [48 48] 39 [41 43]

# -- /notes/in: names and numbers mix
# /notes/in  c3 51 g3 58

# -- /notes/in: a chord with a comma
# /notes/in  [c3, eb3, g3] [c3, eb3, bb3]
# /notes/in  [c3, g3] ~ ~ [eb3, bb3]

# -- /notes/in: a bass line with rests, repeats and euclid
# /notes/in  c2*2 ~ eb2 ~ g2 ~
# /notes/in  c2(3,8) eb2(2,8,1)

# -- /drone/in: frequencies in Hz (65.4 is c2, 98 is g2)
# /drone/in  65.4
# /drone/in  65.4 98 130.8 98
# /drone/in  <65.4 73.4 82.4 98>

# -- /drone/in: a range counts up in whole Hz, so a short one is a slow climb that restarts each cycle
# /drone/in  110 .. 117

# -- /drone/in: a slow pattern over several cycles
# /drone/in  [65.4 98]/2

# -- /cutoff/in: stepped, one value per cycle
# /cutoff/in  <300 600 1200 2400 4800>
# /cutoff/in  <200 8000>

# -- /cutoff/in: per step, several values within a cycle
# /cutoff/in  400 800 1600 3200
# /cutoff/in  [300 3000]*4
# /cutoff/in  500 [800 4000] 600 [1200 6000]

# -- /cutoff/in: a rest keeps the last value
# /cutoff/in  400 ~ 3200 ~
# /cutoff/in  200 ~ ~ ~ 4000 ~ ~ ~
